{"c":[{"id":"920b76cc0b40179f","sum":"R3/G2/L1: event-card misses are event-card code; 'unknown' selection reads as caret; a goal is done only with left[] empty; goal writes pass gates.ts (desk tests: standInJev); never widen drafts.ts restates(); D2-06 scene 2 partial live; no default chat route.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"ba466bbf79b5d07e","sum":"R3/G2: corpus event-card misses are producer code, not the router; context.ts reads 'unknown' selection as a caret. A goal is finished only with left[] empty; goal values are picked by their quoted part, not display.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"362f7f2441a3fcab","sum":"R3: corpus m36/m43 miss event cards by the producer's rule (relative date, no anchor), m37 finds no person: event-card code, not the router. routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as a caret, since RouteFollower sends none then.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T170330Z-9c33f255f5c1caad","text":"R3: corpus m36/m43 list no event card by the producer's rule (a conversation line's relative date has no anchor); m37 finds no person. Those misses are event-card code, not the router.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T170330Z-dcc2d733c48b884a","text":"R3: RouteFollower sends no routingContext while the selection is a plain caret, so routing/context.ts treats the helper's 'unknown' selection as caret; comparing them ended every write session at the host's first sentence end.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e516245b6d5f910e","sum":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only with left[] empty; runs.ts owes every required or recipient field in windows a goal writes. A goal value's display names its source window, so goal-prompt.ts says pick values by their quoted part.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-100b242cff553f5d","text":"G2: GoalProgress finished is done only when left[] is empty (partial/handoff otherwise); runs.ts owes every field left.ts marks required or recipient in windows a goal writes in, and a closed window leaves them unresolved.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173412Z-33695164e4940cad","text":"G2: a goal value's display names its source window's title, so live qwen3.8 matched v.display.includes('ORD-...') to the sender's email; goal-prompt.ts now says pick values by their quoted part.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"6c61dbb360ed9d23","sum":"G2/L1: goal writes pass goals/gates.ts (lowerGoal async, needs askJev + ledger; desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev); never widen drafts.ts restates(); live Jev leaves D2-06 scene 2 partial; no chat route is a default (name groq:/gateway: via --dev-writer).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8febf1c1fb5ea75f","sum":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit, verifyWrites); with no Jev a goal writes no copied value (desk tests use goal-desk.ts standInJev). drafts.ts restates() is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; never widen it by adding words.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T173412Z-c65516aec96de620","text":"G2: every goal write passes goals/gates.ts (never-typed, misfit + numberFieldMisfit, Ask's verifyWrites Jev question); lowerGoal is async and needs askJev + ledger; with no Jev a goal writes no copied value, so desk tests pass test/goal-desk.ts standInJev.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T173413Z-41b9cc8b0f0c0c83","text":"G2: drafts.ts restates() (skip Jev for a restated sentence) is a closed-frame clause-suffix rule; two reviews found 5 bypasses in looser versions (token sets, 'Avoid saying', 'NOT saying', 'provided'); never widen it by adding words.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e10542c624d65f47","sum":"G2: live Jev (0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived event, so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live (evidence/screen/g2). L1: no chat route is a default; developers name groq:<model> or gateway:<model> via --dev-writer.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T180513Z-82a90a8786c261a8","text":"G2: live Jev (Ask's yes/no value question, 0.75 floor) confirmed Order number but not a reply's sender in To or a derived calendar event for 'add this meeting to my calendar and draft a reply to Priya', so D2-06 scene 2 ends partial live; see evidence/screen/g2 jev-*-probe.txt.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T201333Z-b3e261779dc6c92b","text":"L1: no chat route is a default (WRITER_ROUTE and INTENT_ROUTE null, ASK_MAKER jev); a developer names one as groq:<model> or gateway:<model> (writer/routes.ts) with the helper's --dev-writer or an eval script's writer flag.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"5fee49e1dd2634c5","sum":"L1/P1/P2: Gemma E2B drafts need grammar, deadlineMs epoch ms; low-prose labels >80 chars fail; old hosts reject unknown memoryDocument ids; no-groq forbids key reads; add Ask makers to one-answer gate; Label: parts keep context; page-link patches verified writes into last walk.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"31d09dcbe08a45f9","sum":"L1/P1: Gemma E2B base model (few-shot local drafts, grammar required, deadlineMs epoch ms); labelTooLong over 80-char focused labels on low-prose pages; old hosts throw on unknown memoryDocument ids; no-groq.ts fails tests reading GROQ_API_KEY.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"227c87230dc71c8a","sum":"L1: Gemma E2B is a base model (local draft prompts are few-shot; caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar; deadlineMs is epoch ms). Fill throws labelTooLong for a focused label over 80 chars on a page with little prose.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T201333Z-fdcac01d5471b677","text":"L1: Cotypist's Gemma E2B is a base model, so local draft prompts are few-shot documents (writer/local-draft.ts); caret-local-model refuses a request with no grammar. localTextRequest.deadlineMs is epoch ms, not a duration.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T204550Z-12e324b0b44784bf","text":"Fill throws labelTooLong when the focused field's label is over 80 chars on a page with little other prose (privacy prose share); saved answers can't be offered there.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"b818cff7ff0f8991","sum":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id (answers.md is listed only to savedAnswers hosts). P1: test/setup/no-groq.ts fails any test reading process.env.GROQ_API_KEY; pass explicit env objects in tests.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T204550Z-3e3d4d7a0bdec136","text":"Hosts before v2/answers throw on an unknown memoryDocument id, losing the whole memory list; the server lists answers.md only to hosts with the savedAnswers capability.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-7ef033e31edcf1b4","text":"P1: helper/test/setup/no-groq.ts (vitest setupFiles) fails any test file that reads process.env.GROQ_API_KEY, even if the throw is caught; pass explicit env objects to readKey/writersOnStart in tests.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"987201798448cfb5","sum":"P1/P2: recheckFill refused W4 Greenhouse whole (derived Country, no label context); add new Ask makers to planAsk's one-answer gate; parts from a 'Label:' line carry it as context; page-link patches verified writes into the last walk.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"091da897e0ecfee3","sum":"P1: recheckFill refused W4 Greenhouse Fill all whole (Country is a derived part; a control with no label context needs a line equal to its span). The heads Ask maker is one answer: planAsk gates it like the writer; add a new maker name to that gate.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T205140Z-d6ebebc54b7a4ea1","text":"P1: on W4's saved Greenhouse pages Fill all is refused whole by recheckFill (offers/fill-popup.ts ~218): Country 'United States' is a derived part of 'Location: Oakland, California, United States (...)', and a control without label context needs a line equal to the span.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T205140Z-f4ebc7703c97844e","text":"P1: the heads Ask maker (planner/intent-heads.ts) is one answer, so planAsk gates it like the writer (oneAnswer = makerName !== 'jev': inferredAll, listsAll, confirmScope); a new maker name must be added to that gate or its scope stands unconfirmed.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"0584c276559db78d","sum":"P2: a part from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as context; recheckFields drops only failing fields; an unlabelled span in a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it. page-link patches a verified write into the last walk, then walks once later.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T220819Z-519d2cf2c3af807c","text":"P2: a fill part derived from one 'Label: value' line carries that label as FillHandoff.context; recheckFields drops a field that fails its recheck and runs the rest; an unlabelled span inside a longer line passes only if derive.ts re-derives it (fill-popup.ts sourceHolds).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T220819Z-878907191e2eb647","text":"P2: engines/page-link.ts no longer walks after a verified pageWrite/pageSelect/pageSetChecked; it patches that control in the tab's last walk and walks once TRAILING_WALK_MS after the last act. Tests that expected a pageWalk after an ok write must expect the patch.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
